## Emerald vs Cushion vs Round for Men

| Shape | 1ct Natural Price | Clarity Floor | Step Facets | Band Coverage (7mm) | Sophistication Read |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Emerald | [$3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS1 mandatory | Yes — Hall of Mirrors | 100% length × 71% width | Highest — quiet authority |
| Cushion | [$1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS1 recommended | No — brilliant facets | 79% × 79% | High — heritage silhouette |
| Round | [$3,230](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090690?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS2 acceptable | No — brilliant facets | 93% diameter | Neutral — classic |
| **What this means** | Emerald and round similar price | Step facets demand higher clarity | Emerald shows inclusions | Emerald aligns with band length | Emerald is the choice for understated authority |

**Verdict:** Emerald cut costs more than cushion but is comparable to round at natural 1ct. The difference is what it signals. Round is universally correct. Emerald is deliberate — it communicates restraint and confidence. For a men's ring where the stone must project authority without flash, emerald wins. See the [men's cushion cut ring guide](/mens-cushion-cut-ring) and [men's round diamond ring guide](/mens-round-diamond-ring) for direct shape comparisons.

