## Expert Summary

**Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

Emerald cut is the choice for a man who understands what restraint looks like. The step facets don't perform. They reveal. On a wide men's band, that quality is commanding in a way no brilliant cut can replicate.

The 4 Clarity Rules exist because I've seen the same mistakes repeatedly. Men spending $5,836 on a D-IF natural when D-VS1 at $3,140 passes every test at normal viewing distance. That $2,696 belongs on the setting metal or the stone size. VS1 is the floor. VVS and above is wasted on a daily-wear ring.

For lab-grown, the ~2ct IGI F-VVS1 at $2,229 is the best value in this entire men's ring series. Nearly double the face-up at less than the cost of a natural 1ct VS1. Apply Rule 4 and you end up with a more impressive ring for less money.

Pick the stone first. Apply all 4 rules. Then match the setting.

Entry point: [$4,364](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?Genders=men&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a natural GIA VS1 on a men's ridged solitaire. Lab ~2ct option: [$3,961](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29147824?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

